# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — Finance

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns cashflow, budgeting, expense categorization, revenue forecasting, and pricing analysis. AI-first: drafts monthly reports, projects new-agent operating costs (Opus tokens, MCP fees, infra) as input to every `design-agent` proposal so org-chart expansion has visible cost. Finance does NOT set company strategy; surfaces financial evidence the strategy-makers act on.

## Roles

- `finance-lead` — dept lead, owns end-to-end execution. Defined at [`.claude/agents/finance/finance-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/finance/finance-lead.md).

(Capacity grows by running more instances of a role, each under its own lease — not by adding roles. A new role is justified only by a separate zone — its own lease key, labels and processes — and is designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/).)

## Decision rights

Per [`company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md`](../../company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md): decide by **risk class, not rank**. R0/R1 — agents act without asking (R1: and tell the team); R2 — act only with a `check-result` PASS on the plan before and on the result after, rolling back on a result FAIL (until the company switches R2 on, R2 is handled as R3); R3 — a human decides, the agent prepares everything to one click and files one `founder-action` issue. Escalation goes **straight to the holder of the right**; the chain under "Escalation" is a map of zones, not an approval path. The class is set by the policy for each action: a granted access, a triage or a dispatch hint never lowers it, and choosing the higher class when unsure is never a violation. Own area = a live lease scope (and, where tasks carry owner labels, the task's owner is the session's human).

| Class | In this department |
|---|---|
| R0 | models, forecasts, reconciliations, report drafts — every number recomputed from the primary source by the checker before it leaves the department |
| R1 | internal reports to the team, ledger and data files in `data/` |
| R2 | changes in external finance systems once they are registered resources |
| R3 | any payment, any figure a customer sees, pricing, budget commitments, spend above the policy thresholds |

## Escalation

`finance-lead` → `coo` (for process matters) → `ceo` (for material spend authority).

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): expense ledgers, monthly burn-rate reports, pricing analyses, budget projections. May contain redacted vendor data; full vendor PII belongs OUTSIDE this repo — an MCP-gated store is the PLANNED home (Risk 1 hardening path, not yet implemented; until then: keep raw PII out of the repo entirely).
- Cross-dept references: `../../company/strategy/` (read for budget alignment — restricted-data convention applies) and `../../company/policies/` (read for spend-approval policies).

